---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { liveEntries } from '../lib/entries';

const count = (await liveEntries()).length;
---

<Base
  title="About — SharedChats"
  description="SharedChats is an independent, human-curated index of publicly shared AI conversations. Learn what we list, how curation works, and how to reach us."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-10">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">About SharedChats</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
      <p>
        People share remarkable AI conversations every day — brilliant explanations, absurd comedy,
        genuinely impressive technical work — and then those links sink into social feeds and group
        chats. SharedChats is a simple answer to that: a browsable, searchable index of publicly
        shared AI conversations that are actually worth reading. Right now we index
        <strong>{count}</strong> of them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">How curation works</h2>
      <p>
        Every entry starts with a share link that a conversation's author published on an AI
        provider's own site. A human editor reads the conversation and writes an original title,
        summary, and tags. We never copy conversation content — the entry is a signpost, and the
        conversation stays where its author put it. Clicking "Open original chat" takes you to the
        provider's share page.
      </p>
      <p>
        We list what is publicly shared, interesting, and non-harmful. We skip anything exposing
        personal information, and we delist entries promptly when an author or rights holder asks.
        Listing is never endorsement — see our
        <a href="/legal/content-policy/" class="underline">content policy</a> for the details.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">Reach us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, removal requests, or a conversation you think we should see:
        <a href="mailto:hello@sharedchats.com" class="underline">hello@sharedchats.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
